@cc [owner:id13,label:backend] preserve-legacy-shard-routing
The shard-key backfill MUST only fill missing mappings for the main and shadow-write clusters,
using the collection's actual key count through the new-source assignment helper. It MUST reject
assignments that differ from existing legacy routing. It MUST preserve existing mappings and
unrelated config fields. Each added key MUST exist in the cluster's main and any shadow embedder
collection; otherwise the batch MUST fail without writes. It MUST NOT move or modify Qdrant points.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;concurrency] guarded-backfill-writes
Without --execute, the backfill MUST NOT write to PostgreSQL. Execution MUST compare each row's
current config and internal ID with the values read for planning. If any row changed or disappeared,
the entire batch MUST roll back. Successful earlier batches may remain committed and reruns MUST
preserve their stored mappings.
